1
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:18,100
Hey, you're early.

2
00:00:18,476 --> 00:00:20,811
Agent Van Pelt reporting
for the night shift, Marshal Gorman.

3
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:22,605
At ease, Grace.
It's Witness Protection.

4
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:24,065
We're not invading Afghanistan.

5
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:26,067
Yeah, I know, but you know
what the rules say.

6
00:00:26,859 --> 00:00:27,902
Thanks.

7
00:00:29,362 --> 00:00:30,404
Anything I should know?

8
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,241
The Marshals Service
got an anonymous tip.

9
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:35,493
Somebody might be trying to make
a play on Justin tonight.

10
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:38,621
Something to it, you think?

11
00:00:40,581 --> 00:00:43,376
There's always a threat, Grace.
That's how we gotta behave.

12
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:45,461
That's how we keep our guys alive.

13
00:00:47,755 --> 00:00:50,049
- Hey, Grace. I thought that was you.
- Hey, Trina.

14
00:00:50,299 --> 00:00:52,677
Um... I made this picture for you.

15
00:00:55,721 --> 00:00:57,473
It's beautiful. Thank you, Trina.

16
00:00:57,598 --> 00:00:59,267
I love those dogs.

17
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:02,562
Those are horses, Vic. Honestly.

18
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:04,981
Where's your dad?

19
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:07,441
Practicing his testimony
with Ms. Weymouth.

20
00:01:08,025 --> 00:01:10,653
Let me tell ya, he's in a wicked
good mood tonight.

21
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:14,532
- Hey, Grace.
- Hi.

22
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:17,034
- Oh, welcome back, Big Red.
- Focus, Justin.

23
00:01:17,868 --> 00:01:20,288
Mr. DeGeorge, a year ago
you witnessed someone

24
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:21,872
shoot Tanya Matthews in the head.

25
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:24,125
Could you please point out the man
who pulled the trigger?

26
00:01:24,625 --> 00:01:26,752
Right there. Adrian Essex.

27
00:01:27,336 --> 00:01:30,923
You are a money manager, correct?
And Mr. Essex was your client?

28
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:32,133
Yes, he was.

29
00:01:32,592 --> 00:01:34,927
Six months ago,
you were arrested for tax fraud

30
00:01:35,052 --> 00:01:36,262
weren't you, Mr. DeGeorge?

31
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:38,139
But the state offered you a deal.

32
00:01:39,181 --> 00:01:42,059
Yes. In exchange for my testimony
against Essex

33
00:01:42,184 --> 00:01:43,227
I don't go to jail.

34
00:01:43,352 --> 00:01:45,896
Plus, my daughter and I get
Witness Protection.

35
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:49,859
Plus, we get to go over the same
thrilling questions

36
00:01:50,067 --> 00:01:51,944
every single night.

37
00:01:52,278 --> 00:01:53,696
All right. We're done for the night.

38
00:01:54,905 --> 00:01:55,948
Me, too.

39
00:01:56,407 --> 00:01:58,492
I'm off to watch the game
and kiss my dog.

40
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,787
Don't forget,
perimeter sweep, one hour.

41
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:07,668
Agent Van Pelt, the night shift
is officially yours.

42
00:03:18,781 --> 00:03:19,990
"Dispatch here. Go ahead."

43
00:03:20,116 --> 00:03:22,493
This is agent Van Pelt.
I need immediate assistance.

44
00:03:22,785 --> 00:03:24,912
245 in progress
at my current location.

45
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:26,247
"10-4..."

46
00:03:27,456 --> 00:03:29,709
Shots fired. I need backup. Now!

47
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:37,758
Justin?

48
00:03:39,009 --> 00:03:40,052
Trina?

49
00:03:49,478 --> 00:03:50,521
Oh, no.

50
00:03:52,314 --> 00:03:53,357
Trina?

51
00:04:14,001 --> 00:04:15,502
- Anything on the girl?
- Not yet.

52
00:04:15,753 --> 00:04:17,963
- We looking at a kidnapping?
- That or she just ran off.

53
00:04:18,088 --> 00:04:19,923
- Where's the mother?
- Died last year.

54
00:04:20,048 --> 00:04:21,091
It was just Trina and her dad.

55
00:04:21,216 --> 00:04:22,801
All right. Put out an Amber alert
and a BOLO.

56
00:04:22,926 --> 00:04:25,637
Already did. I've set up a perimeter
and notified C.H.P.

57
00:04:25,888 --> 00:04:28,307
{\an8}Good, and one more thing...
get that treated now.

58
00:04:28,682 --> 00:04:29,725
That's an order.

59
00:05:06,178 --> 00:05:07,846
{\an8}We've got ten guys here
five more on their way.

60
00:05:07,971 --> 00:05:10,015
{\an8}- All right. Get going.
- Okay. You guys head that way.

61
00:05:18,774 --> 00:05:19,817
That's...

62
00:05:21,819 --> 00:05:22,861
{\an8}That's it.

63
00:05:25,197 --> 00:05:26,240
Table.

64
00:05:27,866 --> 00:05:28,909
{\an8}Barbecue.

65
00:05:31,453 --> 00:05:34,581
{\an8}- Jane?
- Horribly cold night tonight, Lisbon.

66
00:05:35,123 --> 00:05:36,166
{\an8}Do me a favor, would you?

67
00:05:36,291 --> 00:05:38,752
{\an8}Would you shine your flashlight
up into those treetops?

68
00:05:38,961 --> 00:05:40,796
- Why?
- Because I like the effect

69
00:05:41,004 --> 00:05:43,131
the way the light plays on the leaves.

70
00:05:45,551 --> 00:05:48,262
{\an8}The girl Trina
who made these drawings...

71
00:05:48,679 --> 00:05:50,222
{\an8}They're all from an aerial perspective

72
00:05:50,389 --> 00:05:53,976
{\an8}so my guess is, she has a spot up
high where she works

73
00:05:54,309 --> 00:05:57,563
{\an8}a place where she feels safe
and can hide.

74
00:05:58,188 --> 00:06:00,524
{\an8}- If she wasn't kidnapped.
- Kidnapping. Meh.

75
00:06:00,899 --> 00:06:03,694
{\an8}The man who'd pay her ransom
is lying in a pool of his own blood.

76
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:06,655
{\an8}What do you know, huh?

77
00:06:07,239 --> 00:06:09,366
{\an8}I wonder why you doubt me, Lisbon.

78
00:06:11,034 --> 00:06:12,077
Trina, are you there?

79
00:06:14,621 --> 00:06:16,957
{\an8}Sweetie, it's all right.
We're with the CBI.

80
00:06:17,124 --> 00:06:20,252
{\an8}I know it sounds made up, but we...
we have a web site and everything.

81
00:06:24,882 --> 00:06:26,174
It's all right, Trina.

82
00:06:26,758 --> 00:06:28,719
Just tell us what happened
from the start.

83
00:06:29,011 --> 00:06:31,305
{\an8}I know it's hard, but we really need
your help.

84
00:06:33,932 --> 00:06:35,142
{\an8}She can't do it, Lisbon.

85
00:06:36,184 --> 00:06:37,644
{\an8}She can't remember what happened.

86
00:06:38,562 --> 00:06:39,771
Isn't that right, Trina?

87
00:06:41,356 --> 00:06:42,566
It's all just mixed up.

88
00:06:44,276 --> 00:06:45,611
Has anyone seen my dad?

89
00:06:47,696 --> 00:06:48,739
Trina?

90
00:06:49,615 --> 00:06:52,200
- Aunt Jodie!
- It's okay, baby. It's okay.

91
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:02,336
Hey. Bet you have a bad headache.

92
00:07:02,961 --> 00:07:04,004
Yeah.

93
00:07:04,129 --> 00:07:06,006
Well, that's gonna be a cool scar, though.
There is that.

94
00:07:07,007 --> 00:07:09,217
Van Pelt, you okay? And Trina?

95
00:07:09,927 --> 00:07:11,678
I'm fine. They took Trina to the hospital.

96
00:07:12,054 --> 00:07:13,472
Damn it! I can't believe this.

97
00:07:14,598 --> 00:07:17,100
- This where the son of a bitch got in?
- Well, it's gotta be, right?

98
00:07:17,809 --> 00:07:19,019
The dead bolt's unlocked.

99
00:07:19,895 --> 00:07:21,897
Unless Trina unlocked it
when she ran out.

100
00:07:22,814 --> 00:07:23,857
She couldn't have.

101
00:07:24,107 --> 00:07:27,194
The lock needs a key to get
in or out... this key.

102
00:07:27,903 --> 00:07:29,613
- Did you forget to lock it, Grace?
- Hold on, Nicki.

103
00:07:29,738 --> 00:07:31,448
Agent Van Pelt, when you did
your perimeter sweep

104
00:07:31,573 --> 00:07:33,909
- did you lock that door?
- I-I was starting to

105
00:07:34,034 --> 00:07:36,161
when I heard a noise
in the woods and I just, I think...

106
00:07:39,957 --> 00:07:40,999
I don't know.

107
00:07:42,292 --> 00:07:43,669
I can't remember if I locked it.

108
00:07:45,212 --> 00:07:46,588
Okay. Damage control.

109
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,590
The guy you're looking for
is Adrian Essex.

110
00:07:48,715 --> 00:07:49,841
Major drug trafficker.

111
00:07:50,217 --> 00:07:53,220
We had an airtight murder case.
Victim was our main witness.

112
00:07:53,762 --> 00:07:54,805
Essex will walk.

113
00:07:55,138 --> 00:07:56,807
Well, that's a good motive.
We'll check it out.

114
00:08:03,105 --> 00:08:04,147
"Oh, there you are."

115
00:08:04,606 --> 00:08:06,942
I found a fascinating
clue. Ta-da!

116
00:08:07,234 --> 00:08:08,568
- A matchbook.
- Yes.

117
00:08:08,735 --> 00:08:11,363
The victim collected them
for some ungodly reason.

118
00:08:11,571 --> 00:08:14,741
The question I have for you is why
is this matchbook all alone

119
00:08:14,908 --> 00:08:16,702
and not in the bowl
with the rest of the collection?

120
00:08:16,952 --> 00:08:18,412
Maybe Justin smoked.

121
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:22,207
No ashtray. No cigarettes.
No fumes of tobacco.

122
00:08:22,457 --> 00:08:24,376
I'm leaving.
Wait! Don't touch that!

123
00:08:24,543 --> 00:08:25,836
Forensics hasn't bagged it yet.

124
00:08:26,378 --> 00:08:30,048
Did you know Nevada is both the marriage
and divorce capital of the nation?

125
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:32,092
They should put that on the license plate.

126
00:08:33,385 --> 00:08:34,428
Yeah.

127
00:08:35,345 --> 00:08:37,389
{\an8}Where were you last night
at 10:00 P.M. Mr. Essex?

128
00:08:37,889 --> 00:08:39,349
Your mother gave me a booty call.

129
00:08:39,599 --> 00:08:41,393
Always happy to oblige the old girl.

130
00:08:41,601 --> 00:08:43,645
She's not your type.
So you don't have an alibi then?

131
00:08:43,895 --> 00:08:46,314
I gotta take a leak.
This stuff goes right through me.

132
00:08:46,481 --> 00:08:48,650
DeGeorge isn't the first witness
against you to turn up dead.

133
00:08:49,026 --> 00:08:51,653
- Two years ago, the Leland murder trial?
- How do you do that?

134
00:08:52,195 --> 00:08:53,822
Maybe you got someone
feeding you information.

135
00:08:54,239 --> 00:08:55,449
Just a lucky break.

136
00:08:56,074 --> 00:08:57,743
The guy mixed with a bad set of people.

137
00:08:58,201 --> 00:08:59,911
You do that, bad stuff happens.

138
00:09:00,037 --> 00:09:02,164
I'm gonna ask you one more time.
Where were you last night?

139
00:09:03,582 --> 00:09:06,918
Let me see. I don't rightly recall.

140
00:09:08,211 --> 00:09:09,546
Maybe we should go help you
figure it out.

141
00:09:09,921 --> 00:09:10,964
Against the wall.

142
00:09:15,302 --> 00:09:17,012
Come on. Move.

143
00:09:22,059 --> 00:09:23,101
Oh, yeah.

144
00:09:24,561 --> 00:09:26,021
Ankle monitoring device.

145
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,523
I'm on home confinement during the trial.

146
00:09:29,608 --> 00:09:31,234
Guess I have an alibi after all.

147
00:09:39,284 --> 00:09:41,203
Yeah, seems like an excellent facility.

148
00:09:43,121 --> 00:09:44,164
How's Trina doing?

149
00:09:44,289 --> 00:09:46,792
Physically, she's all right.
Psychologically, it's tricky.

150
00:09:46,917 --> 00:09:49,377
Tricky? Is that a diagnosis?

151
00:09:50,545 --> 00:09:53,173
Trina's memory appears to be fine,
with one exception...

152
00:09:53,298 --> 00:09:55,675
She still has no knowledge
of her father's death.

153
00:09:56,051 --> 00:09:57,385
- You haven't told her yet?
- No.

154
00:09:57,511 --> 00:09:59,763
No, and... and I'm not going to
un-until she's ready.

155
00:09:59,930 --> 00:10:01,348
Until then, please leave her alone.

156
00:10:01,848 --> 00:10:04,017
Ma'am, it's extremely important
that we speak to her.

157
00:10:04,142 --> 00:10:06,686
- She may have witnessed the murder.
- Well, she definitely did.

158
00:10:07,395 --> 00:10:09,856
She's blocking the memory,
because it's too painful.

159
00:10:10,398 --> 00:10:11,608
I can help her remember.

160
00:10:12,442 --> 00:10:13,860
I'll just put her in a light trance.

161
00:10:14,903 --> 00:10:17,447
Hypnosis? Well, that's quackery.

162
00:10:17,614 --> 00:10:20,200
- Well, then it can't hurt to try.
- No.

163
00:10:20,826 --> 00:10:22,702
You're very confident
in what's right for Trina.

164
00:10:23,370 --> 00:10:25,622
You yourself are a medical professional
of some sort.

165
00:10:25,789 --> 00:10:28,917
A nurse, yes? Excellent posture.

166
00:10:29,042 --> 00:10:31,753
I would venture you spent
some time in the armed forces.

167
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,547
- Navy?
- Army.

168
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,632
There's something more, though,
isn't there?

169
00:10:35,966 --> 00:10:38,176
There's a deeper reason
you're so protective.

170
00:10:40,595 --> 00:10:42,931
Trina's mother committed suicide
last year.

171
00:10:43,431 --> 00:10:44,891
She was clinically depressed.

172
00:10:45,976 --> 00:10:47,853
I'm really sorry, ma'am

173
00:10:48,728 --> 00:10:49,771
but we have a job to do.

174
00:10:49,896 --> 00:10:52,774
I'm not gonna tell her
that her father's dead, too

175
00:10:52,899 --> 00:10:54,484
not until she's ready.

176
00:10:54,651 --> 00:10:56,027
Excuse me, doc.
Where's the gift store?

177
00:10:56,236 --> 00:10:57,487
I need to get some reading material

178
00:10:57,612 --> 00:10:59,614
for the car ride home
and a peppermint bar.

179
00:11:00,198 --> 00:11:02,450
I understand that
this is a difficult time for you.

180
00:11:02,617 --> 00:11:05,287
If you just give us five minutes
with her, she'll be fine.

181
00:11:05,453 --> 00:11:06,496
Look, I don't think
you're hearing me, agent.

182
00:11:06,621 --> 00:11:08,039
- I don't think you're hearing me.
- Ladies...

183
00:11:10,125 --> 00:11:11,168
Hey, Trina.

184
00:11:11,793 --> 00:11:12,836
I brought you something.

185
00:11:14,421 --> 00:11:16,381
Talent like yours deserves to be nurtured.

186
00:11:17,632 --> 00:11:19,092
- Talent?
- Oh, come on.

187
00:11:19,217 --> 00:11:20,927
I'm sure you've heard
that from your mom before.

188
00:11:22,304 --> 00:11:23,972
I bet your mother taught you
to draw, right?

189
00:11:25,056 --> 00:11:26,099
How did you know that?

190
00:11:26,224 --> 00:11:29,811
Well, your father's a money manager,
pushes numbers around.

191
00:11:29,978 --> 00:11:32,314
I figured that maybe your mom
is a little more artsy.

192
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:36,484
My mom was a really good artist.

193
00:11:38,278 --> 00:11:39,654
She was the talented one

194
00:11:41,448 --> 00:11:42,490
but she died.

195
00:11:43,408 --> 00:11:45,994
Yeah, I know. I'm sorry.

196
00:11:48,872 --> 00:11:49,915
I have a question.

197
00:11:50,957 --> 00:11:52,000
Your dad smoke?

198
00:11:53,043 --> 00:11:55,086
- No.
- You sure? Interesting.

199
00:11:55,378 --> 00:11:56,922
- Jane?
- Hey.

200
00:11:58,632 --> 00:12:00,133
Are you trying to hypnotize her?

201
00:12:00,759 --> 00:12:02,510
- Hypnotize me?
- I told you no!

202
00:12:02,636 --> 00:12:05,805
The doctor said that her memory
will come back on its own in time!

203
00:12:05,931 --> 00:12:06,973
Back off, tiger.

204
00:12:07,557 --> 00:12:09,893
Easy, all right? I did no such thing.

205
00:12:10,352 --> 00:12:12,229
Wait. Why would he wanna
hypnotize me?

206
00:12:15,941 --> 00:12:17,484
Why won't anyone talk to me?

207
00:12:22,155 --> 00:12:23,657
Aunt Jodie, where's my dad?

208
00:12:25,158 --> 00:12:26,201
Trina...

209
00:12:27,661 --> 00:12:29,829
He hasn't come to see me.
Where is he?

210
00:12:39,381 --> 00:12:40,548
He's dead, isn't he?

211
00:12:42,801 --> 00:12:44,052
Just tell me, please.

212
00:12:46,012 --> 00:12:47,055
Yeah, that's right.

213
00:12:48,556 --> 00:12:49,599
He's dead.

214
00:12:51,768 --> 00:12:52,811
I'm sorry.

215
00:12:53,353 --> 00:12:54,771
He was murdered last night.

216
00:12:59,234 --> 00:13:03,071
Oh, honey. I'm sorry I didn't tell...
I know. It's okay.

217
00:13:03,196 --> 00:13:04,489
It's okay.

218
00:13:08,618 --> 00:13:10,370
Hi. I tried to find you this morning.

219
00:13:10,954 --> 00:13:13,039
Yeah, I'm not really
in the mood for talking.

220
00:13:13,248 --> 00:13:15,292
- I get it, but if you change your mind...
- Grace.

221
00:13:15,875 --> 00:13:17,752
- Craig.
- Hey, I came as soon as I could.

222
00:13:18,336 --> 00:13:19,379
You okay?

223
00:13:21,548 --> 00:13:24,009
- I don't wanna talk about your feelings.
- Good. Me neither. What's up?

224
00:13:24,342 --> 00:13:25,802
Adrian Essex has a number
one enforcer.

225
00:13:25,927 --> 00:13:27,679
Eugene Boden, suspected
in a number of murders.

226
00:13:27,887 --> 00:13:30,223
Essex can't leave the house, but
he can still order the hit. Let's go.

227
00:13:30,557 --> 00:13:32,684
You're being too hard on yourself, okay?

228
00:13:32,809 --> 00:13:34,019
The killer could've picked that lock.

229
00:13:34,144 --> 00:13:35,937
I mean, he, he could've had a key,
for all you know.

230
00:13:36,229 --> 00:13:38,732
Or he didn't need a key
because I maybe left it unlocked.

231
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,068
I lost a witness, Craig.

232
00:13:43,903 --> 00:13:45,155
You're a great cop.

233
00:13:46,281 --> 00:13:47,324
Hey, look at me.

234
00:13:48,241 --> 00:13:49,284
I'm looking.

235
00:13:50,327 --> 00:13:52,662
This will pass. I promise.

236
00:13:55,832 --> 00:13:56,875
I'm interrupting.

237
00:13:59,878 --> 00:14:04,382
Agent LaRoche of professional standards,
this is Craig O'Laughlin, FBI.

238
00:14:06,301 --> 00:14:08,803
The P.S.U. Is looking
into last night's incident.

239
00:14:09,012 --> 00:14:11,431
There are some... questions.

240
00:14:12,140 --> 00:14:14,184
I've scheduled us to meet
this afternoon.

241
00:14:15,018 --> 00:14:17,354
I will need your incident report

242
00:14:17,854 --> 00:14:20,231
and a urine sample to screen
for drugs.

243
00:14:20,774 --> 00:14:23,610
Agent Dubin here will escort you
to the restroom.

244
00:14:25,487 --> 00:14:27,072
- Right now?
- Yes.

245
00:14:31,493 --> 00:14:32,702
Uh, nice meeting you.

246
00:14:43,338 --> 00:14:45,423
"Yeah, just a second.
Joey. Quick."

247
00:14:48,551 --> 00:14:50,804
CBI, Mr. Boden. We need to talk
to you about Justin DeGeorge.

248
00:14:51,054 --> 00:14:52,097
Yeah, I'm a bit busy right now.

249
00:14:52,222 --> 00:14:54,516
You might wanna call my secretary
and make an appointment.

250
00:14:54,682 --> 00:14:55,809
Let us in, sir. It'll just take a second.

251
00:14:55,934 --> 00:14:57,852
I don't think so.
I already told you, I'm busy.

252
00:14:57,977 --> 00:15:00,105
- Hey, let's not make this difficult.
- So piss off. Get out!

253
00:15:09,489 --> 00:15:11,282
Police! Get on the ground now!

254
00:15:11,491 --> 00:15:12,534
Everybody get down!

255
00:15:14,411 --> 00:15:15,453
Get up.

256
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:16,663
Get on your knees.

257
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:20,083
I got it. Go.

258
00:15:21,543 --> 00:15:22,752
"Police! Stop!"

259
00:15:27,257 --> 00:15:28,967
Essex, stop!

260
00:15:32,095 --> 00:15:33,138
Damn!

261
00:15:44,564 --> 00:15:45,606
You look anxious.

262
00:15:47,024 --> 00:15:48,067
Not at all.

263
00:15:49,026 --> 00:15:50,069
No?

264
00:15:50,653 --> 00:15:52,155
It would be understandable.

265
00:15:53,406 --> 00:15:54,615
Agent Van Pelt...

266
00:15:56,576 --> 00:15:59,120
did you leave that door unlocked?

267
00:16:01,956 --> 00:16:02,999
I don't know.

268
00:16:03,291 --> 00:16:07,503
That must be distressing, not knowing
if you're a good cop or not.

269
00:16:14,343 --> 00:16:17,597
You remember Todd Johnson, don't you?

270
00:16:18,431 --> 00:16:22,018
Cop killer murdered here
in our house by one of us.

271
00:16:22,727 --> 00:16:23,769
Why?

272
00:16:24,312 --> 00:16:28,649
I need assistance with my investigation
into his murder.

273
00:16:29,692 --> 00:16:32,403
I need someone trustworthy.

274
00:16:33,362 --> 00:16:34,405
Assistance?

275
00:16:35,490 --> 00:16:38,034
- You have a whole unit.
- I need you.

276
00:16:39,035 --> 00:16:40,077
Me?

277
00:16:42,038 --> 00:16:43,206
Do you have a suspect?

278
00:16:45,791 --> 00:16:46,959
Is it someone I work with?

279
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:52,590
We'll discuss the specifics
at a later point

280
00:16:52,757 --> 00:16:54,342
but essentially all you would
have to do

281
00:16:54,467 --> 00:16:59,013
is keep your eyes open
and at a later point

282
00:16:59,138 --> 00:17:01,557
you might be asked to wear a wire.

283
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,562
You want me to spy
on my own department?

284
00:17:06,687 --> 00:17:09,690
This is your chance
to redeem yourself, agent.

285
00:17:10,399 --> 00:17:12,610
To prove you are a good cop

286
00:17:12,902 --> 00:17:15,905
that you will take down a killer
no matter who it is.

287
00:17:19,116 --> 00:17:20,660
And, of course

288
00:17:20,785 --> 00:17:26,165
it would make my investigation
of your actions much easier

289
00:17:27,959 --> 00:17:29,502
because a good cop

290
00:17:29,794 --> 00:17:32,547
couldn't possibly have left
a door unlocked

291
00:17:33,172 --> 00:17:36,884
and let a witness be killed
in front of his own daughter.

292
00:17:38,302 --> 00:17:39,345
Am I right?

293
00:17:41,430 --> 00:17:42,473
Are you threatening me?

294
00:17:42,723 --> 00:17:46,477
I'm presenting you
with options, agent.

295
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:49,730
Take some time and mull them over.

296
00:17:57,196 --> 00:17:58,739
Your boss is smart.

297
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,993
Essex had this phone rewired
to have the same signal

298
00:18:02,118 --> 00:18:03,202
as the ankle monitor.

299
00:18:03,619 --> 00:18:05,496
Turn the phone on, leave it at home

300
00:18:05,663 --> 00:18:07,081
everybody thinks you're still there.

301
00:18:07,373 --> 00:18:10,793
But Essex forgot one thing...
his neighbor's security cam.

302
00:18:11,002 --> 00:18:14,046
Essex also left his house
the night of DeGeorge's murder.

303
00:18:14,171 --> 00:18:16,382
It makes him look pretty good
for it, don't you think?

304
00:18:16,674 --> 00:18:18,593
Lovely. So I guess I can go then.

305
00:18:19,093 --> 00:18:21,220
I think he's forgetting
that he tried to buy

306
00:18:21,345 --> 00:18:23,931
20 pounds of meth
from the Connera family.

307
00:18:24,056 --> 00:18:25,808
Must be. What kinda price tag
does that carry?

308
00:18:25,933 --> 00:18:26,976
20 years.

309
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:29,562
Won't be too bad.
I hear they're getting HBO in Folsom.

310
00:18:29,729 --> 00:18:32,732
- Get to the point, Mary.
- You and Essex, you came up together.

311
00:18:32,898 --> 00:18:34,859
You've been pulling jobs
with him for the last ten years.

312
00:18:35,151 --> 00:18:36,193
You know where he hides.

313
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:38,112
You give us Essex, we can deal.

314
00:18:38,863 --> 00:18:40,281
It doesn't have to be 20 years.

315
00:18:46,078 --> 00:18:48,456
Tell me more about that... HBO.

316
00:18:50,750 --> 00:18:53,169
Hospital? Why would you say that?

317
00:18:54,211 --> 00:18:56,922
No, I know Aunt Jodie
had banned me from the hospital.

318
00:18:57,298 --> 00:18:59,258
Quite militaristic of her,
don't you think?

319
00:19:00,092 --> 00:19:02,178
Oh. Gotta run. Gotta run.

320
00:19:03,179 --> 00:19:05,264
You're not welcome
at this hospital, Mr. Jane.

321
00:19:05,848 --> 00:19:07,224
That's why I thought I'd find you
out here

322
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:09,685
amongst your, uh, puffing people.

323
00:19:10,353 --> 00:19:12,313
You're trying so hard to quit smoking.

324
00:19:12,897 --> 00:19:15,358
You bite your nails, and you smell
of hand sanitizer

325
00:19:15,483 --> 00:19:18,736
but you are trying to quit for Trina
which I think is admirable.

326
00:19:18,944 --> 00:19:20,905
What do you want?
You are not hypnotizing my niece.

327
00:19:21,030 --> 00:19:23,199
No, no, no. No need to worry
about that.

328
00:19:23,616 --> 00:19:25,076
I'm just going down
through the suspect list

329
00:19:25,201 --> 00:19:28,329
starting with "A" for "Aunt Jodie".

330
00:19:28,996 --> 00:19:31,457
You think I killed Justin...
You've gotta be kidding me.

331
00:19:31,666 --> 00:19:32,708
No.

332
00:19:33,209 --> 00:19:35,127
You're self-possessed.
You're strong-willed.

333
00:19:35,252 --> 00:19:36,962
You believe that violence
can solve problems...

334
00:19:37,088 --> 00:19:38,381
That's the army thing.

335
00:19:38,756 --> 00:19:40,716
I'm a soldier, so I killed him?

336
00:19:41,050 --> 00:19:42,259
Well, you despised him.

337
00:19:43,052 --> 00:19:44,929
You had zero reaction to his death.

338
00:19:45,054 --> 00:19:48,182
Forgive me for being more concerned
with the welfare of my niece.

339
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,562
Go ahead. Light up.
There's no judgment here.

340
00:19:54,188 --> 00:19:55,231
Go on.

341
00:19:57,066 --> 00:19:58,109
Why didn't you like him?

342
00:20:00,945 --> 00:20:02,446
Justin beat my sister.

343
00:20:03,572 --> 00:20:06,283
He'd get drunk and slap her around.

344
00:20:07,284 --> 00:20:09,245
I was overseas.
I couldn't protect her.

345
00:20:10,079 --> 00:20:11,747
So, yes, I did hate him.

346
00:20:12,289 --> 00:20:13,332
When Molly...

347
00:20:13,958 --> 00:20:15,918
when she died, I moved here.

348
00:20:16,502 --> 00:20:18,462
I was going to fight him
for custody of Trina.

349
00:20:23,509 --> 00:20:27,012
So there you go. Maybe I did
have motive for killing the bastard.

350
00:20:29,056 --> 00:20:30,099
Nice lighter.

351
00:20:32,977 --> 00:20:34,353
Your sister Molly...

352
00:20:35,563 --> 00:20:36,647
where did you say she died?

353
00:20:36,897 --> 00:20:39,817
A no-tell motel in Reno.
It's pathetic.

354
00:20:40,735 --> 00:20:42,778
A hopeless place to kill yourself.

355
00:20:44,321 --> 00:20:45,948
I was so angry at her for that.

356
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:51,370
I'm sorry, Jodie.
I seem to have misjudged you.

357
00:20:51,495 --> 00:20:53,998
Please let me make amends.
Look at me.

358
00:20:56,542 --> 00:20:59,295
Every time you breathe
a breath of that putrid smoke

359
00:20:59,462 --> 00:21:00,504
remember this.

360
00:21:01,297 --> 00:21:06,010
There's a fat, rich tobacco executive
thinking what a fool you are

361
00:21:06,552 --> 00:21:08,888
every time you breathe that smoke

362
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,514
laughing at you

363
00:21:10,890 --> 00:21:14,018
with his fat jowls wobbling
with glee.

364
00:21:14,727 --> 00:21:17,188
- Do you see him?
- Yeah.

365
00:21:32,953 --> 00:21:35,790
- Oh. Sorry. I didn't order that.
- No, I-I did.

366
00:21:36,749 --> 00:21:37,792
Thank you.

367
00:21:39,251 --> 00:21:40,294
It's your favorite.

368
00:21:41,003 --> 00:21:43,297
Come on. And chocolate always makes
you feel better when you're upset.

369
00:21:43,714 --> 00:21:46,008
Mm-hmm. I need to work
on my poker face, huh?

370
00:21:47,176 --> 00:21:48,219
Yep.

371
00:21:48,928 --> 00:21:50,137
I'm betting it's LaRoche.

372
00:21:52,431 --> 00:21:53,474
Spill.

373
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:55,392
Pass that over here.

374
00:22:04,485 --> 00:22:06,320
He wants me to spy
on my department

375
00:22:06,445 --> 00:22:07,988
or he'll go after me.

376
00:22:08,864 --> 00:22:10,533
Is this about that cop-killer murder?

377
00:22:11,909 --> 00:22:13,035
I don't know what to do.

378
00:22:14,245 --> 00:22:15,287
I'm sorry, babe.

379
00:22:16,747 --> 00:22:18,082
This is never fun.

380
00:22:19,333 --> 00:22:20,751
But, look, someone in your organization

381
00:22:20,876 --> 00:22:22,711
set a man on fire and let him burn alive.

382
00:22:23,128 --> 00:22:25,381
Look, even if you knew who he was,
wouldn't you turn him in anyway?

383
00:22:27,216 --> 00:22:28,467
Yeah, I guess I would.

384
00:22:28,843 --> 00:22:31,136
Okay. Well, isn't that all
LaRoche is asking you to do?

385
00:22:31,387 --> 00:22:33,973
- To catch the guy?
- Craig, these are my friends.

386
00:22:34,515 --> 00:22:37,017
How am I supposed to wear
a wire while I talk to a friend?

387
00:22:38,143 --> 00:22:41,230
They're your colleagues, okay?
I'm your friend.

388
00:22:41,939 --> 00:22:43,691
I'm the one who's here for you
no matter what.

389
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:47,820
I get it.
It's a tough call.

390
00:22:48,863 --> 00:22:50,155
Okay, so whatever you decide

391
00:22:51,198 --> 00:22:52,658
just know that I love you

392
00:22:53,450 --> 00:22:54,702
okay, and I'm behind you.

393
00:22:57,079 --> 00:22:58,122
Okay.

394
00:23:00,124 --> 00:23:01,500
All right. Now have some chocolate.

395
00:23:06,547 --> 00:23:10,885
E-s-s-e-x. Adrian Essex.
Yes, that's the guy.

396
00:23:11,010 --> 00:23:12,052
Let me know if you get a hit.

397
00:23:14,889 --> 00:23:16,348
Is that the Justin DeGeorge file?

398
00:23:16,682 --> 00:23:18,601
Yeah, and guess what I found in it.

399
00:23:18,893 --> 00:23:20,352
DeGeorge called the police last year

400
00:23:20,477 --> 00:23:22,062
claimed that Trina's Aunt Jodie
attacked him.

401
00:23:22,271 --> 00:23:24,565
Not surprising. He abused her sister.

402
00:23:24,732 --> 00:23:26,525
Says who?
Records say nothing about that.

403
00:23:26,734 --> 00:23:27,985
Well, that's records for you.

404
00:23:28,152 --> 00:23:30,696
Oh, there's stuff in here
about Trina's mother. Excellent.

405
00:23:31,238 --> 00:23:34,366
Any leads on Essex yet?
My CIs are all quiet as mice.

406
00:23:34,617 --> 00:23:35,868
Rigsby's got squat.

407
00:23:36,994 --> 00:23:39,788
C.H.P, Border patrols, airports...

408
00:23:39,914 --> 00:23:41,457
they've all got pictures of the guy.
We've just gotta wait.

409
00:23:41,749 --> 00:23:44,251
I'm also getting a warrant out
on Essex's finances.

410
00:23:44,418 --> 00:23:47,087
If he paid for the hit on DeGeorge
then maybe we have a trail.

411
00:23:47,338 --> 00:23:49,924
Did you know it used to be illegal
to celebrate Christmas in Boston?

412
00:23:50,132 --> 00:23:53,177
Yeah. Pilgrims thought the whole
spectacle rather debauched.

413
00:23:53,802 --> 00:23:54,845
Didn't know that.

414
00:23:55,429 --> 00:23:58,015
Got something.
A list of every property Essex owns.

415
00:23:58,182 --> 00:23:59,808
- Good place to start looking.
- Great.

416
00:24:00,100 --> 00:24:01,894
I'll get my guys on it.
Should take a couple hours.

417
00:24:02,311 --> 00:24:04,438
Oh, sounds a little tedious.
Do you mind if I take a peek?

418
00:24:04,855 --> 00:24:06,398
If we can get Essex and Boden
in a lineup

419
00:24:06,523 --> 00:24:08,192
then we'll see what's what
and who's the killer.

420
00:24:08,317 --> 00:24:10,527
A lineup for who, Trina?
She can't remember anything.

421
00:24:10,653 --> 00:24:13,739
Well, the doctor says certain
stimulus can jog memories.

422
00:24:13,948 --> 00:24:15,407
That's great, but we don't have Essex.

423
00:24:15,658 --> 00:24:17,242
Well, I've got 100 bucks
that says I can figure out

424
00:24:17,368 --> 00:24:18,869
where Essex is in less than a minute.

425
00:24:20,329 --> 00:24:21,372
Pass.

426
00:24:21,580 --> 00:24:22,623
A minute from now.

427
00:24:22,831 --> 00:24:24,875
- Can I get in on this?
- Oh, yeah. Come on, baby.

428
00:24:32,174 --> 00:24:34,176
Up! Up! Listen to me, you ogre.

429
00:24:34,677 --> 00:24:38,347
I ask only this... Follow my finger.

430
00:24:38,472 --> 00:24:40,808
- What the hell?
- You're telling me where your boss hides.

431
00:24:40,933 --> 00:24:43,560
- Oh, come on. Give me a break.
- Who doesn't like a break?

432
00:24:44,019 --> 00:24:46,438
A nice cold beer after a long, hard day

433
00:24:47,106 --> 00:24:49,066
put your feet up on the big, comfy sofa.

434
00:24:49,233 --> 00:24:51,652
Relaxes you, soothes you.

435
00:24:52,152 --> 00:24:53,195
A break is a good thing.

436
00:24:54,655 --> 00:24:56,156
I'm... I'm done with this.

437
00:24:56,907 --> 00:24:58,075
So am I. Splendid.

438
00:25:02,329 --> 00:25:03,914
- Time?
- 27 seconds.

439
00:25:04,707 --> 00:25:05,749
"And here we go."

440
00:25:05,874 --> 00:25:07,793
You will find Essex at 9 Eagle Drive.

441
00:25:08,711 --> 00:25:09,837
Come on. No way.

442
00:25:10,129 --> 00:25:12,339
When I put my finger
over the correct address

443
00:25:12,464 --> 00:25:13,841
Boden couldn't help but react.

444
00:25:13,966 --> 00:25:17,636
His lips tightened.
His nostrils flared ever so slightly.

445
00:25:17,928 --> 00:25:18,971
Classic tells.

446
00:25:19,221 --> 00:25:20,514
I'll get S.W.A.T. ready.

447
00:25:22,349 --> 00:25:24,435
- Wicked good job, if you're right.
- Thanks.

448
00:25:24,893 --> 00:25:26,520
But I'm not paying up
until the guy's in cuffs.

449
00:25:26,645 --> 00:25:28,439
Well, just so you know, I prefer cash.

450
00:25:33,986 --> 00:25:35,446
You guys set?
Let's roll.

451
00:25:36,155 --> 00:25:37,197
Go. Split. Three and three.

452
00:26:06,060 --> 00:26:07,311
Freeze! CBI!

453
00:26:19,531 --> 00:26:20,574
Move!

454
00:26:20,949 --> 00:26:21,992
Damn.

455
00:26:34,338 --> 00:26:35,380
Gun!

456
00:26:36,340 --> 00:26:39,343
Move! Move! Get out of the way!
Damn it.

457
00:26:43,972 --> 00:26:45,015
Drop it, Essex.

458
00:26:45,682 --> 00:26:46,725
Do it now.

459
00:26:55,025 --> 00:26:56,068
Hands on your head.

460
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,243
Let's go.

461
00:27:12,791 --> 00:27:15,293
I wanna make our position clear
from the outset.

462
00:27:15,502 --> 00:27:17,170
We are not interested in a plea.

463
00:27:17,295 --> 00:27:19,673
My client is innocent of every charge.

464
00:27:19,923 --> 00:27:20,966
That right?

465
00:27:21,133 --> 00:27:23,969
Sure, Adrian had the ability
to leave his house

466
00:27:24,261 --> 00:27:26,763
but in no way does that prove
that he killed Justin DeGeorge.

467
00:27:26,888 --> 00:27:28,390
He snuck out the night of the murder.

468
00:27:28,515 --> 00:27:30,725
My girlfriend hurt her back,
so I went to see her.

469
00:27:30,976 --> 00:27:32,477
- She'll swear to it.
- Naturally.

470
00:27:32,686 --> 00:27:34,938
There's also a drug charge.
20 pounds of meth in that house.

471
00:27:35,188 --> 00:27:36,898
But Adrian wasn't in the same room

472
00:27:37,023 --> 00:27:38,650
and Mr. Boden will testify
that my client

473
00:27:38,775 --> 00:27:39,901
had no knowledge of the drugs.

474
00:27:40,068 --> 00:27:41,111
Your client evaded arrest.

475
00:27:41,236 --> 00:27:44,072
Only after the CBI agents
illegally forced their way in.

476
00:27:44,197 --> 00:27:45,240
That was by the book.

477
00:27:45,782 --> 00:27:46,825
That's debatable.

478
00:27:47,868 --> 00:27:50,036
There were no drugs in plain sight

479
00:27:50,162 --> 00:27:52,164
no exigent circumstances
to enter the home.

480
00:27:52,831 --> 00:27:55,709
Trust me. I get much better evidence
thrown out every day

481
00:27:55,917 --> 00:27:57,002
for a lot less.

482
00:27:58,128 --> 00:28:00,005
We need to put Trina in front
of a lineup.

483
00:28:00,213 --> 00:28:02,299
We've got both Boden and Essex
in custody.

484
00:28:03,258 --> 00:28:05,093
I'm sorry.
I'm afraid that won't be possible.

485
00:28:05,886 --> 00:28:06,928
Please, ma'am.

486
00:28:25,780 --> 00:28:28,617
What is he doing?
Could you please control your man?

487
00:28:28,783 --> 00:28:30,452
Oh, believe me, she's tried.

488
00:28:30,827 --> 00:28:33,705
I-I think a lineup
is a ridiculous waste of time.

489
00:28:33,830 --> 00:28:36,833
- She doesn't remember anything.
- A lineup might jog her memory.

490
00:28:38,168 --> 00:28:40,587
Hi, Trina. You wanna I.D.
your father's killer?

491
00:28:42,547 --> 00:28:44,841
D-did you just ask her
to come down here?

492
00:28:45,467 --> 00:28:47,510
This is... unconscionable.

493
00:28:47,636 --> 00:28:50,805
On the contrary, it's totally conscionable.
We can conscion this very easily.

494
00:28:52,182 --> 00:28:53,225
I'll do it.

495
00:28:53,850 --> 00:28:55,435
No, honey.
Honey, I...

496
00:28:56,436 --> 00:28:58,438
I'm not gonna let you become
a witness, okay?

497
00:28:58,563 --> 00:29:00,106
I-I won't put you in danger.

498
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:01,483
We'll protect her.

499
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:03,735
Like you protected her father?

500
00:29:04,694 --> 00:29:06,154
Go ahead. Tell your aunt.

501
00:29:08,365 --> 00:29:10,700
It's my dad who died, not yours.

502
00:29:12,661 --> 00:29:14,329
- If you won't let me do this
- Trina...

503
00:29:14,454 --> 00:29:16,122
I'll never forgive you, I swear.

504
00:29:19,459 --> 00:29:20,502
Fine.

505
00:29:20,710 --> 00:29:21,753
Okay then.

506
00:29:33,390 --> 00:29:34,516
All right. Bring 'em in.

507
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:39,104
Now remember, Trina,
you can see them

508
00:29:39,271 --> 00:29:40,313
but they can't see you.

509
00:29:46,736 --> 00:29:47,779
Turn to the right.

510
00:29:52,659 --> 00:29:54,202
Now, turn to the left.

511
00:30:00,625 --> 00:30:01,668
And face center.

512
00:30:05,964 --> 00:30:07,299
Do any of them look familiar?

513
00:30:12,095 --> 00:30:14,222
- I'm sorry.
- You don't have to be sorry.

514
00:30:14,472 --> 00:30:15,598
You did the best you could.

515
00:30:16,099 --> 00:30:17,809
Rigsby, you wanna get Jodie
started on the paperwork

516
00:30:17,976 --> 00:30:19,227
so we can get Trina outta here?

517
00:30:19,436 --> 00:30:21,146
- Paperwork?
- Yeah, you know, the, uh...

518
00:30:21,354 --> 00:30:24,524
- Form Y2Ks and the, uh...
- The standard minor release forms.

519
00:30:24,941 --> 00:30:27,444
- It shouldn't take long.
- Sure. Yeah. Uh, right this way.

520
00:30:27,569 --> 00:30:29,195
Hey, honey.
I'll be back in a minute, okay?

521
00:30:29,529 --> 00:30:30,572
Okay.

522
00:30:32,741 --> 00:30:34,284
Whatever you're doing,
you're not doing it alone.

523
00:30:34,409 --> 00:30:35,660
Such little faith.

524
00:30:36,536 --> 00:30:37,954
You wanna catch your father's killer?

525
00:30:38,496 --> 00:30:39,539
Let me help.

526
00:30:40,373 --> 00:30:41,416
Okay.

527
00:30:41,541 --> 00:30:43,793
All you have to do is trust me.
Can you do that?

528
00:30:53,053 --> 00:30:54,095
- Finally.
- Yeah.

529
00:30:56,639 --> 00:30:58,475
Oh. I'm sorry.

530
00:30:59,267 --> 00:31:00,894
You used blue pen.
You have to kinda use black.

531
00:31:01,019 --> 00:31:03,355
- They're real sticklers about this.
- You're kidding me.

532
00:31:03,563 --> 00:31:06,274
Oh, Janet. Essex's bank records?
Thank you. Finally.

533
00:31:06,858 --> 00:31:10,111
Rigsby, stand guard over Trina.
Nobody gets in or out of that room.

534
00:31:10,779 --> 00:31:12,197
Wait a minute. What happened?
What's going on?

535
00:31:12,781 --> 00:31:14,324
Trina remembered
what happened that night.

536
00:31:14,491 --> 00:31:15,992
What the hell is he talking about?

537
00:31:16,284 --> 00:31:17,577
I hypnotized your niece.

538
00:31:18,870 --> 00:31:21,289
- You son of a bitch!
- Who's the killer?

539
00:31:22,165 --> 00:31:23,333
She hasn't told us yet.

540
00:31:23,666 --> 00:31:25,126
She's still piecing it together
in her mind.

541
00:31:25,251 --> 00:31:26,378
It's a very complicated process

542
00:31:26,544 --> 00:31:28,088
but we'll know who the killer
is soon enough.

543
00:31:28,380 --> 00:31:30,590
How could you do this?
How could you let him?

544
00:31:30,715 --> 00:31:33,468
We are gonna take her
to a safe place immediately.

545
00:31:34,135 --> 00:31:36,763
I'll call my director.
Anything you want, you've got.

546
00:31:37,013 --> 00:31:38,723
I've got a great Witsec
apartment downstate.

547
00:31:38,890 --> 00:31:39,933
We can keep her there long-term.

548
00:31:41,726 --> 00:31:43,228
How do you sleep at night?

549
00:31:43,645 --> 00:31:45,772
Most nights I don't,
but I give you my word

550
00:31:45,897 --> 00:31:48,066
I will not let anything bad
happen to Trina.

551
00:31:48,233 --> 00:31:50,610
Yeah? You better hope you don't.

552
00:32:10,797 --> 00:32:12,257
Yeah, everything's clear.

553
00:32:12,549 --> 00:32:13,800
Trina's fast asleep.

554
00:32:14,968 --> 00:32:16,010
No problem, boss.

555
00:32:31,901 --> 00:32:33,611
- Freeze!
- Jesus!

556
00:32:34,070 --> 00:32:36,281
- Drop the weapon, Gorman!
- You scared the crap outta me.

557
00:32:36,448 --> 00:32:37,490
Get down on the ground.

558
00:32:38,324 --> 00:32:39,367
What are you talking about?

559
00:32:39,951 --> 00:32:42,078
I just came by to see
if, uh, Trina was okay.

560
00:32:42,412 --> 00:32:43,955
Trina's safe elsewhere.

561
00:32:44,330 --> 00:32:46,374
We know you came here
to kill her.

562
00:32:46,749 --> 00:32:47,792
Are you outta your mind?

563
00:32:48,042 --> 00:32:51,463
Essex hired you tonight,
like he hired you to kill her father.

564
00:32:53,173 --> 00:32:55,258
You know me, Grace.
We've been working together for weeks.

565
00:32:55,383 --> 00:32:58,595
- Give up the weapon now!
- Just, just wait a second.

566
00:32:58,928 --> 00:33:01,347
Just hold on a second.
I did not kill Justin.

567
00:33:01,848 --> 00:33:04,350
- Three, two, one...
- Okay! All right. Calm down.

568
00:33:04,517 --> 00:33:06,519
I'm putting the gun down.
All right?

569
00:33:26,621 --> 00:33:28,539
We found a key
in Gorman's apartment

570
00:33:28,748 --> 00:33:30,625
to the dead bolt at Justin's house.

571
00:33:31,834 --> 00:33:34,128
I didn't leave that door unlocked.
He did.

572
00:33:35,588 --> 00:33:36,631
I am a good cop.

573
00:33:38,508 --> 00:33:39,842
So it would seem.

574
00:33:42,887 --> 00:33:46,224
The investigation
into your actions is over.

575
00:33:47,266 --> 00:33:50,186
And as to the other matter,
I decline your offer.

576
00:33:51,062 --> 00:33:52,480
I won't spy on my friends.

577
00:33:54,524 --> 00:33:57,276
A killer works in the CBI.

578
00:33:58,444 --> 00:34:00,905
Every day you pass
each other in the halls.

579
00:34:01,405 --> 00:34:02,782
You share information.

580
00:34:03,407 --> 00:34:06,035
You might well put your life
into this person's hands.

581
00:34:07,828 --> 00:34:09,330
I find that bothersome

582
00:34:09,705 --> 00:34:11,541
but you seem fine with it.

583
00:34:15,461 --> 00:34:16,504
Are we done?

584
00:34:17,922 --> 00:34:18,965
We are.

585
00:34:25,805 --> 00:34:26,931
- Hey.
- Hey.

586
00:34:27,515 --> 00:34:29,559
- I'm proud of you.
- Aw. Thanks.

587
00:34:30,726 --> 00:34:32,019
So how about I take you to lunch?

588
00:34:32,603 --> 00:34:34,105
I have something special planned.

589
00:34:35,022 --> 00:34:36,399
- Yeah. All right.
- Yeah?

590
00:34:37,608 --> 00:34:39,485
You paid Gorman to kill Justin

591
00:34:39,735 --> 00:34:41,821
and when you realized
Trina could I. D. Gorman

592
00:34:41,946 --> 00:34:43,197
you put a hit out on her, too.

593
00:34:43,322 --> 00:34:44,949
Yeah, like you can prove that.

594
00:34:45,616 --> 00:34:46,826
Did you get this from the girl?

595
00:34:47,118 --> 00:34:49,745
Anything she says under hypnosis
is inadmissible.

596
00:34:49,870 --> 00:34:52,748
Oh. Oh. No, no, no.
I never hypnotized Trina.

597
00:34:53,291 --> 00:34:55,418
Much to the relief of her aunt, I must say

598
00:34:55,918 --> 00:34:57,336
Trina never remembered anything.

599
00:34:57,503 --> 00:35:00,923
I did it to lure Gorman out,
and it worked a treat.

600
00:35:01,424 --> 00:35:02,967
And we do have the proof

601
00:35:03,301 --> 00:35:05,845
and not just the bag of meth
we found at Gorman's

602
00:35:06,178 --> 00:35:07,763
but also your bank records.

603
00:35:08,097 --> 00:35:10,391
You paid Gorman 10 grand
for each hit.

604
00:35:10,933 --> 00:35:12,393
Every time Gorman made a deposit

605
00:35:12,518 --> 00:35:13,936
the same amount came out
of your account.

606
00:35:14,061 --> 00:35:16,689
- What are the chances?
- In the six years Gorman worked for you

607
00:35:16,814 --> 00:35:19,734
it looks like you commissioned
five murders.

608
00:35:19,900 --> 00:35:21,944
It seems like we're gonna close
some open cases.

609
00:35:22,361 --> 00:35:24,488
And I think he's gonna look great
in an orange jumpsuit.

610
00:35:24,655 --> 00:35:27,366
So if the girl didn't say anything to you,
how did you get on to Gorman?

611
00:35:27,533 --> 00:35:29,702
That lovely hockey Jersey.
You're from Boston.

612
00:35:30,953 --> 00:35:32,788
Oh, come on.
It's wicked obvious.

613
00:35:33,497 --> 00:35:34,957
Gorman's also from Boston.

614
00:35:35,541 --> 00:35:37,168
You guys even grew up
on the same block.

615
00:35:37,376 --> 00:35:39,045
Yeah. How do you like them apples?

616
00:35:47,887 --> 00:35:50,473
Hey. Congratulations. I heard.

617
00:35:50,848 --> 00:35:51,891
You did? Already?

618
00:35:53,267 --> 00:35:56,270
Oh, the P.S.U. investigation.
Right.

619
00:35:56,687 --> 00:35:59,023
- Sorry. I thought...
- Thought what?

620
00:36:01,192 --> 00:36:02,693
I thought you heard my news already

621
00:36:02,818 --> 00:36:06,072
and I really wanted to tell you myself.

622
00:36:11,035 --> 00:36:13,496
Craig asked me to marry him,
and I said yes.

623
00:36:19,543 --> 00:36:23,297
That's wonderful, Grace.
That's terrific news.

624
00:36:23,547 --> 00:36:24,590
He's a great guy.

625
00:36:26,175 --> 00:36:27,218
Thank you, Wayne.

626
00:36:28,552 --> 00:36:29,595
I...

627
00:36:32,598 --> 00:36:34,225
- Thanks.
- Yeah.

628
00:36:46,529 --> 00:36:48,739
Hi. Thank you for coming.
I-I don't know what's wrong.

629
00:36:48,864 --> 00:36:51,659
Not at all. I brought Lisbon along
on account of you don't trust me

630
00:36:51,992 --> 00:36:53,703
despite the fact that I helped
her quit smoking.

631
00:36:53,828 --> 00:36:54,870
Now that's gratitude.

632
00:36:56,205 --> 00:36:58,541
- In there.
- No good deed goes unpunished.

633
00:37:06,924 --> 00:37:08,217
You remember now, don't you?

634
00:37:09,468 --> 00:37:10,511
Remember what?

635
00:37:13,597 --> 00:37:14,974
It's okay. You can say.

636
00:37:15,933 --> 00:37:17,226
You're safe here.

637
00:37:20,521 --> 00:37:22,106
I remember what happened.

638
00:37:24,984 --> 00:37:26,026
I did it.

639
00:37:26,861 --> 00:37:27,903
It was me.

640
00:37:31,031 --> 00:37:32,533
What is she talking about?

641
00:37:33,033 --> 00:37:34,910
It was Trina who shot her father.

642
00:37:35,911 --> 00:37:39,874
No. No. That Marshal shot Justin.
That's what you said.

643
00:37:41,083 --> 00:37:43,711
Well, technically Gorman
was hired to kill Justin.

644
00:37:43,836 --> 00:37:47,006
"He snuck onto the property
but he never got to the killing part."

645
00:37:55,389 --> 00:37:56,432
"What?"

646
00:37:57,683 --> 00:38:00,019
But Gorman's killed a lot of other
people so, meh, you know...

647
00:38:00,686 --> 00:38:01,729
good riddance.

648
00:38:03,814 --> 00:38:05,649
Essex didn't know
that Gorman had failed.

649
00:38:05,775 --> 00:38:07,109
He paid him for the hit.

650
00:38:07,693 --> 00:38:11,739
Exactly. That's why Gorman
came after Trina.

651
00:38:12,823 --> 00:38:15,701
He couldn't very well explain to Essex
that he'd cheated him

652
00:38:16,410 --> 00:38:17,703
because she was the killer.

653
00:38:20,998 --> 00:38:23,417
Trina, why?

654
00:38:27,588 --> 00:38:28,923
Justin murdered her mother.

655
00:38:30,841 --> 00:38:32,092
It-it was suicide.

656
00:38:32,551 --> 00:38:34,970
Justin got these from a bar in Reno...

657
00:38:35,930 --> 00:38:37,348
where Molly died.

658
00:38:38,307 --> 00:38:40,142
And according to his case file

659
00:38:40,309 --> 00:38:42,561
he told police he had
never been to Reno.

660
00:38:53,572 --> 00:38:57,159
"I was just looking for something
to light a candle when I..."

661
00:38:59,119 --> 00:39:00,412
I found these.

662
00:39:02,915 --> 00:39:05,376
"I-I don't get it, Dad.
You said you've never been there."

663
00:39:08,712 --> 00:39:09,755
"Come here!"

664
00:39:10,881 --> 00:39:11,924
"Give me that!"

665
00:39:16,011 --> 00:39:17,263
"Your mother thought
she could leave me"

666
00:39:17,471 --> 00:39:18,514
"and take you with her like..."

667
00:39:18,764 --> 00:39:21,267
- "like I'm some kinda schmuck!"
- "Ow! Dad, you're hurting me!"

668
00:39:22,226 --> 00:39:23,894
"I swear to God, you say one word"

669
00:39:24,103 --> 00:39:25,980
"one word, you will end up
the same way."

670
00:39:26,355 --> 00:39:27,481
"Are you gonna make me do that?"

671
00:39:28,107 --> 00:39:29,233
"Answer me, girl!"

672
00:39:30,025 --> 00:39:32,111
"Answer me! Answer me!"

673
00:39:36,699 --> 00:39:38,492
- "Hey!"
- "Aah! Don't!"

674
00:39:45,583 --> 00:39:47,459
I'm so sorry.

675
00:39:49,795 --> 00:39:51,380
We need to talk. Now.

676
00:40:03,017 --> 00:40:05,311
You knew. You knew the whole time.

677
00:40:05,436 --> 00:40:09,231
Um... not the whole time, no.
Hang on. What are you doing?

678
00:40:09,356 --> 00:40:10,691
I'm calling juvenile services.

679
00:40:10,858 --> 00:40:12,693
I don't want them to take her
to county for booking.

680
00:40:12,860 --> 00:40:14,278
Really? That's your plan for this girl?

681
00:40:14,403 --> 00:40:15,571
- Jail?
- Give me the phone, Jane!

682
00:40:15,696 --> 00:40:16,864
No, I can't.

683
00:40:17,823 --> 00:40:20,492
She took somebody's life.
She confessed to a police officer.

684
00:40:20,618 --> 00:40:23,495
For God sakes, Lisbon,
the girl's father was an abuser.

685
00:40:23,662 --> 00:40:25,456
So was mine! I didn't shoot him!

686
00:40:27,333 --> 00:40:28,417
It was self-defense.

687
00:40:30,002 --> 00:40:32,880
Exactly. And if it was
self-defense, she'll be acquitted.

688
00:40:33,047 --> 00:40:34,590
Oh, and the courts never get it wrong.

689
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,592
The system never chews people up.

690
00:40:36,717 --> 00:40:39,595
We are the system, Jane.
We get it right most of the time.

691
00:40:39,845 --> 00:40:41,680
Okay, so she's proven innocent.

692
00:40:41,889 --> 00:40:44,099
How much time do you think
she's gonna spend in foster care?

693
00:40:44,308 --> 00:40:45,809
Six months? A year?

694
00:40:48,312 --> 00:40:50,940
- I don't know.
- It's all so unnecessary, isn't it?

695
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:53,525
'Cause Trina's aunt is a nurse.

696
00:40:53,734 --> 00:40:56,570
Aunt Jodie can get her
the psychiatric help that she needs...

697
00:40:56,820 --> 00:40:58,364
Help, not punishment.

698
00:41:00,032 --> 00:41:02,034
We don't get to pick
who gets a pass and who doesn't.

699
00:41:02,159 --> 00:41:03,911
- That is the job of the courts.
- Please.

700
00:41:04,078 --> 00:41:05,996
And our job,
our job is to catch the killer.

701
00:41:06,121 --> 00:41:08,207
What happens after that
is up to other good people

702
00:41:08,332 --> 00:41:10,292
who are also doing the best job
they can.

703
00:41:13,504 --> 00:41:16,215
Damn it. Why did she confess?

704
00:41:17,341 --> 00:41:18,425
Because she's a good person.

705
00:41:23,514 --> 00:41:24,556
We don't have to do this.

706
00:41:26,058 --> 00:41:27,601
We can let her go just this once.

707
00:41:28,686 --> 00:41:29,812
Just once.

708
00:41:43,117 --> 00:41:44,410
"All right. Let's go, ladies."

709
00:41:49,957 --> 00:41:51,000
Don't be scared.

710
00:42:01,093 --> 00:42:02,136
What do we got?

711
00:42:10,227 --> 00:42:11,437
It's okay, Teresa.

712
00:42:13,063 --> 00:42:14,940
Ho, we're busy here, lady.

713
00:42:20,738 --> 00:42:21,864
Keep up the good work.

714
00:42:24,742 --> 00:42:26,827
Trina, we're gonna take you home.

715
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:34,752
You just witnessed a beautiful thing.
